{
 "_about": "One action table for the three harnesses (review finding F6), version 4: the read rules are ordered in groups, so that no `!` exception can reopen a secret file another rule denies. The generator (`security::actions`) builds the Claude permission arrays, the delegate settings fragment and the Codex rules file from it, and fails when a family lacks an entry or a stated reason for any harness. Grok reads the Claude command rules from .claude/settings.json (grok-build f0e3be11: xai-grok-workspace/src/permission/resolution.rs:28-68). Text rules are defense in depth: exec-guard parses the unwrapped argv for every family here, and the guard hooks fail closed (departure D8).",
 "families": [
  {
