   "codex_note": "An attached `--receive-pack=` or `--exec=`, `gh secret list` and an `ext::` remote cannot be a Codex prefix without forbidding every `git push` or `gh secret`; git-guard and exec-guard's outward check carry them."
  },
  {
   "id": "forge_write",
   "decision": "ask",
   "why": "A `gh api` call that writes (a POST, PUT or PATCH method in any spelling, a field or an input body, separated or attached, or any GraphQL call, since a mutation and a query share one form), a call with a short-option bundle (`-i` is the only flag that can lead one), and a call to another host (`--hostname`) run outside the Claude sandbox by name (TSK-1070). They prompt in every mode, bypass included; an unattended session is refused (ADR-0093, departing from ADR-0075 decision 1 for this family only). These text rules name the common spellings only: exec-guard reads every `gh api` call by gh's own option grammar, in any case, bundle or `=` form, answers Claude Code with the same prompt for each write, absolute URL and `--hostname` call, and refuses a form it cannot read (TSK-1070 security review round 2).",
   "claude": [
