 "startup_paths": {
  "why": "Shell startup files and the files that run commands when a shell or terminal starts (issue 86, TSK-242), with CodeFlow's launcher files under `~/.codeflow` (TSK-1070): the `claude` function and the editor wrapper run at every shell or editor start, the session file sets what every later CodeFlow session may do, and the install records decide what an uninstall removes. A function or alias planted in one is loaded by every later shell, and every command-text guard then judges the name it sees, not what runs. No policy key relaxes the class: the user edits their own profile. An entry ending in `/` is a directory and everything below it. `home` entries are relative to the home; the zsh entries also apply under `ZDOTDIR` and the `.config/` entries under `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` when those are set for the guard. `absolute` entries are system files. `anywhere` entries are file names protected in every directory.",
  "home": [
   ".bashrc",
   ".bash_profile",
   ".bash_login",
   ".profile",
   ".bash_logout",
   ".bash_aliases",
   ".bashrc.d/",
   ".bash_completion",
   ".bash_completion.d/",
   ".inputrc",
   ".zshenv",
   ".zprofile",
   ".zshrc",
   ".zlogin",
   ".zlogout",
   ".zshenv.zwc",
   ".zprofile.zwc",
   ".zshrc.zwc",
   ".zlogin.zwc",
